<title>USA: Mikasa Inc Q1 sales rise, net income falls.</title>
<headline>Mikasa Inc Q1 sales rise, net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONG BEACH, Calif. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOR THE THREE MONTHS Ended March 31,     1997	     1996</p>
<p>Net sales by channel of distribution:</p>
<p>   Direct to consumers		     $ 39,062	$ 33,622</p>
<p>   Retail accounts			     28,981	  29,846</p>
<p>   International				  5,065	   5,752</p>
<p>     Total					 73,108	  69,220</p>
<p> Cost of sales				   40,336	  38,471</p>
<p>   Gross profit				  32,772	  30,749</p>
<p> SG&amp;A						32,061	  28,872</p>
<p>   Income from operations			 711	   1,877</p>
<p> Interest expense, net			    216	     212</p>
<p>   Income before income taxes		   495	   1,665</p>
<p> Income tax provision			     191	     658</p>
<p>   Net income					 304	   1,007</p>
<p> Net EPS					     0.02	    0.05</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs				   18,359	  22,280</p>
<p>		   (In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said comparable sales of retail stores for Q1 1997 up 2.9 percent. Sales to retail accounts fell 2.9 percent. It said costs related to store openings affected profitability for the quarter, with substantial sales to offset these costs anticipated in the second half of the year.</p>
</text>
